{"slug":"/students/subjects/physics/mechanics/work-energy-power/","source":"students/subjects/physics/mechanics/work-energy-power.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Work, Energy & Power | Physics Mechanics","description":"","subject":"physics","body":"<div class=\"max-w-6xl mx-auto\">\n        <nav class=\"mb-8\">\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/mechanics/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700\">← Back to Mechanics</a>\n        </nav>\n\n        <div class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-8\">\n            <header class=\"mb-12\">\n                <h1 class=\"text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Work, Energy &amp; Power</h1>\n                <p class=\"text-lg text-gray-600\">Understanding the relationships between work, energy, and power in mechanical systems</p>\n            </header>\n\n            <div class=\"grid gap-8\">\n                <!-- Work -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Work</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\">\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Definition &amp; Formula</h3>\n                                <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n                                    <li>• W = F·d·cos θ</li>\n                                    <li>• Units: Joules (N·m)</li>\n                                    <li>• Scalar quantity</li>\n                                    <li>• Can be positive or negative</li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div>\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Special Cases</h3>\n                                <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n                                    <li>• Zero work: Force perpendicular to displacement</li>\n                                    <li>• Maximum work: Force parallel to displacement</li>\n                                    <li>• Negative work: Force opposes displacement</li>\n                                    <li>• Work by gravity: mgh (independent of path)</li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Energy -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Energy</h2>\n                    <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\">\n                        <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                            <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Kinetic Energy</h3>\n                            <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n                                <li>• KE = ½mv²</li>\n                                <li>• Energy of motion</li>\n                                <li>• Always positive</li>\n                                <li>• Depends on mass and velocity</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                            <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Potential Energy</h3>\n                            <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n                                <li>• Gravitational: PE = mgh</li>\n                                <li>• Elastic: PE = ½kx²</li>\n                                <li>• Stored energy</li>\n                                <li>• Reference point dependent</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Conservation of Energy -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Conservation of Energy</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\">\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Law Statement</h3>\n                                <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n                                    <li>• Total energy remains constant</li>\n                                    <li>• Energy cannot be created/destroyed</li>\n                                    <li>• Can be converted between forms</li>\n                                    <li>• Valid in isolated systems</li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div>\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Applications</h3>\n                                <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n                                    <li>• Pendulum motion</li>\n                                    <li>• Roller coasters</li>\n                                    <li>• Spring oscillations</li>\n                                    <li>• Free fall</li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Power -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Power</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\">\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Definition &amp; Formulas</h3>\n                                <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n                                    <li>• P = W/t (work per time)</li>\n                                    <li>• P = F·v (force × velocity)</li>\n                                    <li>• Units: Watts (J/s)</li>\n                                    <li>• Instantaneous vs. average power</li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div>\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Real-World Examples</h3>\n                                <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n                                    <li>• Engine power ratings</li>\n                                    <li>• Electrical appliances</li>\n                                    <li>• Human power output</li>\n                                    <li>• Industrial machinery</li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Problem-Solving Examples -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Problem-Solving Examples</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <div class=\"space-y-6\">\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Example 1: Roller Coaster</h3>\n                                <p class=\"text-gray-700\">A roller coaster car starts from rest at height h. Find its velocity at the bottom.</p>\n                                <div class=\"mt-2 pl-4 text-sm text-gray-600\">\n                                    <p>Solution approach:</p>\n                                    <ol class=\"list-decimal pl-4 space-y-1\">\n                                        <li>Initial energy (all potential)</li>\n                                        <li>Final energy (all kinetic)</li>\n                                        <li>Apply conservation of energy</li>\n                                        <li>Solve for velocity</li>\n                                    </ol>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Example 2: Power Calculation</h3>\n                                <p class=\"text-gray-700\">Calculate the power needed to lift a 50kg box 2m in 3 seconds at constant velocity.</p>\n                                <div class=\"mt-2 pl-4 text-sm text-gray-600\">\n                                    <p>Key points:</p>\n                                    <ul class=\"list-disc pl-4 space-y-1\">\n                                        <li>Work against gravity</li>\n                                        <li>Constant velocity means constant power</li>\n                                        <li>Use P = W/t</li>\n                                    </ul>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Practice Problems -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Practice Problems</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <ol class=\"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-4 text-gray-700\">\n                            <li>\n                                <p class=\"font-medium mb-2\">Spring System</p>\n                                <p>A 2kg mass is attached to a spring with k = 100 N/m. Find the maximum velocity if compressed 10cm.</p>\n                            </li>\n                            <li>\n                                <p class=\"font-medium mb-2\">Inclined Plane</p>\n                                <p>Calculate work done pushing a 5kg box up a 30° incline for 4m with friction coefficient 0.2.</p>\n                            </li>\n                            <li>\n                                <p class=\"font-medium mb-2\">Power Output</p>\n                                <p>An athlete runs upstairs, gaining 10m elevation in 5 seconds. Calculate power output if athlete mass is 70kg.</p>\n                            </li>\n                        </ol>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-50 to-indigo-100 p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }\n        .content-card {\n            -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(16px);\n            backdrop-filter: blur(16px);\n            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);\n            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n            box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);\n        }"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}